\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. STAND, soldier of the Cross,
\par Thy high allegiance claim,
\par And vow to hold the world but loss
\par For Thy Redeemer's name.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Arise, and be baptized,
\par And wash thy sins away;
\par Thy league with God be solemnized,
\par Thy faith avouched to-day.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. No more thine own, but Christ's-
\par With all the saints of old,
\par Apostles, seers, envangelists,
\par And martyr throngs enrolled-
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. In God's whole armour strong,
\par Front hell's embattled powers:
\par The warfare may be sharp and long,
\par The victory must be ours.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. O bright the conquerer's crown,
\par The song of triumph sweet,
\par When faith casts every trophy down
\par At our great Captain's feet!\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

